# The keys qa/.env.local may provide. qa/.env.local is never committed. Every key is optional: a
# variable in the shell wins over qa/.env.local, which wins over the default shown.
#
# Automated QA runs against the QA instance only (decision 099): SALON_LOCAL_INSTANCE=qa, web 3200,
# API 8190, PostgreSQL 5540, state in .local/qa/ under the product root. Start it with
#   SALON_LOCAL_INSTANCE=qa infra/scripts/local-up.sh
# The QA instance's ports never come from the root .env (which describes the default instance), and
# a run aimed at a default-instance port (3100, 8090, 5440) or at SALON_LOCAL_INSTANCE other than qa
# refuses to start.
# SALON_LOCAL_INSTANCE=qa
# SALON_API_PORT=8190
# SALON_WEB_PORT=3200
# SALON_POSTGRES_PORT=5540
# QA_API_URL=http://localhost:8190
# QA_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3200

# Accounts: the fixed roster, infra/local/accounts.json of the product root (password 123456@321,
# public by decision 099), plus extra accounts a test seeds and removes. Nothing here is a secret.

# The checkout whose running QA instance is under test (its infra scripts, .local/qa/ state and
# roster), when it is not this checkout. Its absolute root:
# QA_PRODUCT_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/the/checkout/running/the/qa/instance
